          "source_quote": "οὐ γὰρ ἦσαν ὑπὸ τῶν παρθένων ἐπιδεδομένοι, οὐδὲ διὰ τῆς πύλης παρενηνεγμένοι.",
          "english_quote": "The virgins had not handed them over or carried them through the gate.",
          "issue": "The simplified sentence makes the virgins the explicit agent of both negated actions. The selected source separately denies that the stones had been brought through the gate, without restricting that denial to carriage by the virgins. The English therefore permits a possibility the source excludes: passage through the gate by someone else. The standard edition preserves this separate negation, but the simplified main text does not.",
